cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >
  FireWatch Colombia: spatiotemporal audit of thermal source
  classification in VIIRS active fire detections
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Vásquez Castro"
    given-names: "Néstor Oswaldo"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-6483-790X"
    affiliation: "Universidad Central, Bogotá, Colombia"
version: 0.1.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22565857"
date-released: "2026-09-06"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/nvasquezc/firewatch-colombia"
abstract: >
  Regional audit of the thermal source classification embedded in the NASA
  FIRMS VIIRS 375 m active fire product over Colombian territory. Detections
  are aggregated onto a metric grid in the national reference system and
  characterized by persistence descriptors: recurrence rate, monthly
  coverage, radiometric stability and circular concentration over the annual
  cycle. Cells labelled by the provider as volcanoes or static land sources
  serve as a verified positive set, allowing discriminant power to be
  calibrated without manual annotation. The study tests whether presumed
  vegetation fire detections contain a separable subpopulation of persistent
  anthropogenic thermal sources absent from the global mask, and quantifies
  the resulting bias in national burned area statistics.
keywords:
  - active fire detection
  - VIIRS
  - remote sensing
  - spatiotemporal analysis
  - thermal anomalies
  - product validation
  - Colombia